+# Status guidance (ADR-027). Each rule restates what ModelEnv already requires for a GROUNDED declaration; nothing
+# here reveals a task's answer. "trained" is the exact prompt AGENT-V1/V2 were fine-tuned on (byte-identical, keep
+# it for reproducing those runs and for building training data); "guided" adds how to read the solve report.
+GUIDANCE = (
+    " How to read your last solve report (last_solve) - always for the model you have NOW (after any add/remove, "
+    "solve again before declaring): "
+    "status 'empty_model': search the target and add fragments. "
+    "status 'solved' with target_value and no context_violations, validity_failures or closure_violations: declare "
+    "determined with value = target_value copied exactly; if any of those lists is non-empty, repair first. "
+    "status 'underdetermined': the diagnostics name the free variables ('specify k of [...]'); if the library has a "
+    "fragment whose context matches the problem that links one of them, search it, add it and solve again; if no "
+    "such fragment exists, the problem is underdetermined - declare underdetermined. "
+    "status 'conflict' or non-empty closure_violations: declare contradictory unless a wrong-context or invalid "
+    "fragment caused it (then remove it and solve again). "
+    "status 'invalid_domain' or non-empty validity_failures: declare outside_validity unless a different fragment "
+    "valid for this problem replaces the failing one. "
+    "status 'ambiguous': declare ambiguous. "
+    "status 'not_converged' or 'no_root': no solution was found; never invent a value - revise the model or declare "
+    "what the evidence supports. "
+    "non-empty context_violations: remove those fragments; nothing is grounded while they are in the model. "
+    "Solving an unchanged model returns the same report: never repeat an action that changed nothing. If the "
+    "observation contains 'feedback', your recent actions made no progress - follow it.")
+PROMPTS = {"trained": LLMModelPolicy.SYSTEM, "guided": LLMModelPolicy.SYSTEM + GUIDANCE}
+
+
+def model_messages(obs: dict, prompt: str = "trained") -> list[dict]:
+    return [{"role": "system", "content": PROMPTS[prompt]},
             {"role": "user", "content": json.dumps(obs, default=str, sort_keys=True)}]
diff --git a/docs/ARCHITECTURE_DECISIONS.md b/docs/ARCHITECTURE_DECISIONS.md
index b37f891..d1bb9e7 100644
--- a/docs/ARCHITECTURE_DECISIONS.md
+++ b/docs/ARCHITECTURE_DECISIONS.md
@@ -338,3 +338,29 @@ through the current environment (`batch_runner.replay`); episodes the current en
 are re-run, so one table never mixes two environment versions. The scoring policy is printed in summary.md.
 **Limits.** Multi-start is not a proof of non-existence (hence `not_converged`, never `no_root`, for coupled
 blocks); the start grid is fixed (<= 48 starts); ambiguity among coupled roots is detected only when stage 1 fails.
+
+### ADR-027 — ModelEnv no-progress guard and solve-status guidance — Accepted
+
+**Evidence.** Real M1 run, model_seen (40 tasks): 6 correct, 11 wrong, 23 budget_exhausted, mean 31.8 steps. In
+`beam_underdetermined#0` the model searched delta, added `cantilever_end_load_deflection`, solved (underdetermined:
+specify 1 of ['I', 'delta']) and then issued `solve` for the remaining 37 steps. The observation is stateless
+(problem, model, last search, last solve, steps_left): an unchanged solve returns a byte-identical observation, so
+nothing told the model that its action had no effect.
+**Decision.** (1) State = (model, last search, last solve). A non-declare action is *no-progress* if the state after
+it was already visited this episode (unchanged re-solve, repeated search, add/remove cycles, malformed actions).
+(2) At 2 consecutive no-progress actions the observation gains `feedback` (streak, unchanged solver status and
+diagnostics, what to do instead, how many more end the episode). (3) At 5 the episode ends: outcome `no_progress`,
+reward -1 (the budget_exhausted convention). Any new state resets the streak; the guard never declares and never
+rewards (non-terminal reward stays 0). Thresholds are `ModelEnv.no_progress_warn/stop`. Reward version
+`modelenv-r2`. (4) Prompt versions: `trained` (exact AGENT-V1/V2 fine-tuning prompt, default of `model_messages`,
+used for training data) and `guided` (= trained + how to read each solve status; eval default,
+`--model-prompt`). Prompt version is part of the policy name (`llm:<gen>+guided`), recorded in the manifest, and
+resume re-runs episodes recorded under another prompt. (5) Per-episode `no_progress` stats (actions, warnings,
+max_streak, recovered, stopped) are summarised per suite and printed in summary.md, separate from infra_error.
+**Effect on references.** Constructor: unchanged (0 no-progress actions; trajectories equal the recorded E5
+episodes). Greedy retrieval, model_seen: 12 correct / 28 wrong -> 8 correct / 12 wrong / 20 no_progress: its 4
+heat_underdetermined successes came only from idling ~32 steps until `steps_left <= 3`, and 16 loop-then-wrong
+episodes now stop earlier. model (held-out): 16/8 -> 16 correct / 8 wrong / 4 no_progress (nozzle_thrust).
+**Limits.** `guided` is off the AGENT-V1/V2 training distribution; compare generations under the same prompt and use
+`--model-prompt trained` to reproduce trained-prompt numbers. Episodes that never repeat a state see observations
+identical to r1.
